---
module: resource_loading
func_id: indent-included-templates
---

***conformance tests***

# indented-includes
With `implement.plain` holding the three lines `something nice and useful`, `    - the nice thing should be really nice`, `    - the useful thing should be really useful`, and `template.plain` holding `- This is a functionality inside a template.`, rendering:
```
- Implement {% raw %}{% include "implement.plain" %}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}{% include "template.plain" %}{% endraw %}
    {% raw %}{% include "template.plain" %}{% endraw %}
    - Implement {% raw %}{% include "implement.plain" %}{% endraw %}
```
gives:
```
- Implement something nice and useful
    - the nice thing should be really nice
    - the useful thing should be really useful
- This is a functionality inside a template.
    - This is a functionality inside a template.
    - Implement something nice and useful
        - the nice thing should be really nice
        - the useful thing should be really useful
```
- The loaded templates are exactly `implement.plain` and `template.plain` with their sources.

# include-in-comment-is-kept
Rendering the line `> This is a with an include tag {% raw %}{% include "template.plain" %}{% endraw %}` gives `> This is a with an include tag {% raw %}{% include 'template.plain' %}{% endraw %}`.

# arguments-are-variables
With `t.plain` holding `Hello {% raw %}{{ name }}{% endraw %}`, rendering `{% raw %}{% include 't.plain', name: 'Ann' %}{% endraw %}` gives `Hello Ann`.

***acceptance tests***
